"""Accounting-based hypothesis coverage and externally challenged mechanisms.
Curated primary-source facts; classification does not identify causal effects.
"""
from pathlib import Path
import json,csv,datetime,hashlib
ROOT=Path(__file__).resolve().parents[1];OUT=ROOT/'workstreams/extension_hypotheses';OUT.mkdir(parents=True,exist_ok=True)
questions=[
('EX01','Information improves consideration','Look separately for hypothetical choice and completed purchases; a null field result challenges guaranteed conversion.','H05,H15,H19,H20,H24'),
('EX02','Battery evidence improves a resale decision','Separate technical evidence, perceived usefulness, willingness to pay, appraiser acceptance and completed transaction price.','H09,H24'),
('EX03','Cash timing matters independently of nominal price','Look for timing-preference evidence and distinguish tax incentives from vehicle-loan insurance financing.','H05'),
('EX04','A vehicle or charging directory solves access','Challenge proximity with source quality, eligibility and boundary definitions.','H06,H11,H25'),
('EX05','Digital activity produces incremental contribution','Distinguish eligible need, dealer capture, contribution per job and additional/displaced costs; cross-check all original hypotheses.','H01-H25')]
plan={'created_utc':datetime.datetime.now(datetime.timezone.utc).isoformat(),'label':'Prespecified follow-up questions; earlier results and some new source discovery already known. Not blind preregistration.','questions':[dict(zip(['test_id','proposition','challenge','hypotheses'],x)) for x in questions],'scope':'Finite accounting and lifecycle coverage, not every cause or every web source. No Auto2000 intervention or implementation.'}
planpath=OUT/'FOLLOWUP_QUESTIONS.json'
if not planpath.exists():planpath.write_text(json.dumps(plan,indent=2))

# One primary accounting component per hypothesis, with secondary links.
# Capture dominates the original hypothesis set; this imbalance is reported.
groups={
 'A':{'title':'Eligible job opportunities','definition':'Vehicle-period population times job eligibility and incidence, before dealer choice.'},
 'B':{'title':'Completed dealer capture','definition':'Share of eligible jobs actually completed at the relevant Auto2000 entity, after customer decisions and operational handoffs.'},
 'C':{'title':'Contribution per completed job','definition':'Job revenue less the direct costs recognized in gross profit, including product/work mix and actual payer. Each cost is assigned once.'},
 'D':{'title':'Additional cost, displacement and risk','definition':'Counterfactual resource, capacity and risk checks. Operating costs below gross profit remain separate; displacement already reflected in completed volumes is not subtracted again.'}}
primary={1:'A',2:'B',3:'B',4:'B',5:'B',6:'B',7:'A',8:'A',9:'B',10:'B',11:'B',12:'D',13:'B',14:'B',15:'B',16:'B',17:'B',18:'B',19:'B',20:'B',21:'B',22:'C',23:'D',24:'B',25:'A'}
secondary={1:'B',2:'D',3:'A,D',4:'D',5:'A,C',6:'A',7:'B,C',8:'C',9:'C,D',10:'C',11:'D',12:'B',13:'C,D',14:'A,C',15:'D',16:'A,D',17:'D',18:'D',19:'D',20:'A,D',21:'D',22:'A,B',23:'B,C',24:'C,D',25:'B,C'}
hs=json.loads((ROOT/'reports/hypothesis_assessment.json').read_text());rows=[]
for h in hs:
 n=int(h['hypothesis_id'][1:]);g=primary[n]
 rows.append({'hypothesis_id':h['hypothesis_id'],'hypothesis':h['initial_hypothesis'],'primary_accounting_component':g,'component_name':groups[g]['title'],'secondary_component_links':secondary[n], 'observable_status_first_wave':h['assessment_status'],'causal_mechanism_status':'unresolved','missing_observation':h['remaining_identification_gap'],'rival':h['initial_rival']})
assert len(rows)==25 and len({x['hypothesis_id'] for x in rows})==25
with (OUT/'MECE_HYPOTHESIS_COVERAGE.csv').open('w',encoding='utf8',newline='') as f:
 w=csv.DictWriter(f,fieldnames=list(rows[0]));w.writeheader();w.writerows(rows)

sources=[
{'id':'EXT-H-S01','authors':'Petrov, I.; Carroll, J.; Denny, E.','year':2025,'title':'Communicating car costs: Results from stated and revealed preference experiments','url':'https://doi.org/10.1016/j.trd.2025.104921','primary_locator':'Publisher-indexed abstract, discussion and conclusion; Transportation Research Part D 147, 104921. DOI redirect failed in read tool; original publisher search text available.','design':'Irish online discrete choice experiment and showroom randomized controlled trial','observed_endpoint':'Hypothetical drivetrain choice versus actual showroom car choices','finding':'Longer-horizon monetary cost information affected hypothetical BEV choice; the showroom trial did not detect an overall effect on drivetrain choice or efficiency/emissions of cars sold.','limits':'A null detected effect in this setting is not proof of zero effect everywhere. No verified Auto2000 effect size or portable uplift.','hypothesis_links':['H05','H15','H19','H20'],'transferability':'Mechanism counterevidence, not Indonesian effect estimation.'},
{'id':'EXT-H-S02','authors':'Bernardic, U.; Cerruti, D.; Filippini, M.; Savelsberg, J.; Ugazio, G.','year':2024,'title':'De-biasing electric vehicle adoption with personalized nudging','url':'https://doi.org/10.3929/ethz-b-000663125','primary_locator':'ETH Zurich working paper 24/390 and author-hosted abstract; UK sample described in official presentation.','design':'Randomized information experiment with 3,181 car owners; working paper','observed_endpoint':'Stated purchase preference, not confirmed vehicle delivery','finding':'Personalized driving/parking-based information, especially TCO, increased BEV purchase preference in the reported experiment.','limits':'Working-paper evidence; selection and foreign context; preferences do not establish sales, margins or branch adoption.','hypothesis_links':['H05','H15','H24'],'transferability':'Supports plausibility of personalized fit information while leaving commercial realization unresolved.'},
{'id':'EXT-H-S03','authors':'Gore, C.; Iogansen, X.; Kneifel, J.; Helveston, J. P.','year':2025,'title':'Data Collection Instrument: Consumer Valuation of Battery Health Information in Used Electric Vehicle Markets','url':'https://doi.org/10.6028/NIST.DCI.008','primary_locator':'NIST DCI 008, abstract PDF p4 and survey instrument; November2025.','design':'Proposed survey and discrete choice instrument','observed_endpoint':'Study design, not reported estimated price premium','finding':'The instrument varies ordinary used-car attributes and battery-specific information to investigate valuation. It does not itself report a measured certificate premium.','limits':'Cannot be cited as completed causal evidence that certification raises trade-in offers.','hypothesis_links':['H24'],'transferability':'A useful distinction between a research question and a result.'},
{'id':'EXT-H-S04','authors':'Webb, D.; Gore, C.; Kneifel, J.','year':2025,'title':'Consumer Perspectives on Battery Electric Vehicles: An Analysis of Battery Information and Knowledge','url':'https://doi.org/10.6028/NIST.TN.2328','primary_locator':'NIST TN2328, abstract PDF p4; validated sample printed p8/PDF16; survey design printed p4; question wording printed p6.','design':'2023 U.S. survey of1,490 individuals, including490 BEV owners','observed_endpoint':'Perceived usefulness, concerns and stated next-vehicle likelihood','finding':'Respondents found battery lifetime/range information useful; source questions distinguish guarantee, federal rating, manufacturer warranty and industry rating.','limits':'Neither actual appraiser acceptance nor a causal transaction-price premium is measured. Source-specific sample differs from other NIST analyses.','hypothesis_links':['H09','H24'],'transferability':'Information types are separable; magnitude is not an Indonesian estimate.'},
{'id':'EXT-H-S05','authors':'Roberson, L. A.; Helveston, J. P.','year':2022,'title':'Not all subsidies are equal: Measuring preferences for electric vehicle financial incentives','url':'https://doi.org/10.1088/1748-9326/ac7df3','primary_locator':'Author-hosted original abstract; Environmental Research Letters17,084003.','design':'U.S. conjoint survey of2,170 respondents','observed_endpoint':'Stated valuation of incentive design','finding':'Immediate rebates were valued more than delayed or differently delivered tax benefits, with subgroup differences.','limits':'Tax incentives differ from financing insurance premiums. No dollar value or policy effect is transferred to Auto2000.','hypothesis_links':['H05'],'transferability':'Qualitative support for separating timing and nominal amount.'},
{'id':'EXT-H-S06','authors':'Roberson, L. A.; Pantha, S.; Helveston, J. P.','year':2024,'title':'Battery-powered bargains? Assessing electric vehicle resale value in the United States','url':'https://doi.org/10.1088/1748-9326/ad3fce','primary_locator':'Author-hosted original abstract; Environmental Research Letters19,054053.','design':'Published observational analysis of roughly9million U.S. online used-car listings2016-2022','observed_endpoint':'Listing values and modeled retention, not necessarily completed transaction prices','finding':'Retention patterns vary by model year, range and brand, while incentives and market shocks also matter.','limits':'The9million rows were used by that study, not acquired by this project. Listed value differs from transaction price; no Indonesian certificate effect.','hypothesis_links':['H24','H25'],'transferability':'Challenges a battery-only explanation of resale value.'},
{'id':'EXT-H-S07','authors':'Loh, W. S.; Noland, R. B.','year':2024,'title':'Concerns expressed by used electric vehicle owners based on surveying social media','url':'https://doi.org/10.1016/j.trd.2024.104086','primary_locator':'Rutgers authors institutional publication record and original publisher abstract.','design':'Survey recruited through used-EV Facebook/Reddit communities, Sep-Oct2022;1,669responses,1,167usable','observed_endpoint':'Reported concerns among self-selected U.S. used-EV owners','finding':'Price, battery performance and public charging are prominent concerns; lower-income concern differs.','limits':'This is a recruited survey, not passive social-media scraping or a representative Indonesia sample. Underlying Rutgers data page returned403; raw survey was not acquired.','hypothesis_links':['H05','H24','H25'],'transferability':'Highlights household heterogeneity and survivor/selection limits.'}
]
(OUT/'EXTERNAL_MECHANISM_EVIDENCE.json').write_text(json.dumps(sources,indent=2))
with (OUT/'EXTERNAL_MECHANISM_EVIDENCE.csv').open('w',encoding='utf8',newline='') as f:
 w=csv.DictWriter(f,fieldnames=list(sources[0]));w.writeheader();w.writerows({**s,'hypothesis_links':','.join(s['hypothesis_links'])} for s in sources)
coverage={g:sum(r['primary_accounting_component']==g for r in rows) for g in groups}
out={'groups':groups,'primary_counts':coverage,'coverage_complete_for_original25':True,'primary_assignments_unique':True,'cross_links_are_not_additional_hypotheses':True,'external_primary_studies_or_instruments':len(sources),'new_raw_customer_rows_from_these_studies':0,'plan_sha256':hashlib.sha256(planpath.read_bytes()).hexdigest(),'limits':'MECE for accounting categories under a stated business perimeter, not causal independence or exhaustive knowledge.'}
(OUT/'MECE_COVERAGE_QA.json').write_text(json.dumps(out,indent=2))
md=['# MECE accounting and evidence that can challenge the mechanism','','A consistent business perimeter and period come first. For each vehicle/job cohort, gross profit is eligible opportunities times completed dealer capture times job gross profit (revenue less recognized direct cost per completed job), summed across mutually exclusive jobs. Incremental gross profit is the difference between the with-change and counterfactual totals. Operating costs below gross profit belong in a separate initiative-cost comparison. Each direct cost, discount, benefit, recovery and risk obligation needs one ledger location. If displaced jobs or channel cannibalization are already reflected in the all-channel counterfactual volumes, do not subtract them again. The factors interact; these are analytical categories, not four additive profit pools or independent causal explanations.','','Each original hypothesis has one primary accounting location and secondary links. This prevents counting a duplicated hypothesis as multiple independent findings. It does not force a customer journey, a cause and a financial line into one hierarchy. Lifecycle, powertrain, payer and decision-owner labels are separate dimensions.','','## Coverage of the original hypothesis set','']
for g,detail in groups.items():md += [f"{g}. {detail['title']}: {coverage[g]} primary hypotheses. {detail['definition']}",'']
md+=['The original set is concentrated on capture. Customer reach and digital friction therefore receive more hypotheses than measured incidence or contribution per job. That is a coverage imbalance, not evidence that capture is the largest profit problem. Safety recalls, off-network economical repair and vehicle/organization exit are additional lifecycle topics identified in the parallel MECE review.','','## New external mechanism checks','']
for s in sources:
 md += [f"### {s['id']}: {s['title']}",f"{s['finding']} {s['limits']}",f"Design and endpoint: {s['design']}. {s['observed_endpoint']}.",f"Source: {s['authors']} ({s['year']}). {s['url']}",'']
md+=['## What changes in the diagnosis','','Personalized cost/fit information remains plausible. A guaranteed sales uplift is not justified by stated-choice success, especially alongside an undetected showroom effect in the Irish study. A null detected result does not prove that the true effect is zero. Those studies do not identify an Auto2000 effect. Information should be analyzed separately from liquidity, product fit, decision timing, adviser behavior and fulfillment.','','Battery evidence has at least five distinct links: technically valid measurement, understandable presentation, credible source, acceptance by the decision owner, and a changed transaction. A digital certificate establishes none of the later links automatically. NIST usefulness evidence and an instrument for future valuation research cannot fill an unobserved appraiser or transaction-price link.','','The large resale study supports heterogeneity rather than a battery-only explanation: vehicle age/model/range, broader market conditions and incentive history may all change residual value. A condition certificate cannot insure every one of those risks. Its9million listings are not included in this project or counted as our datapoints.','','## Acquisition boundaries','','The Rutgers survey repository returned403 and the author-linked resale replication archive returned429. No login, proxy bypass or repeated forcing of either route was used. GitHub discovery led to the author publication page and its independently published archive link; it did not yield the9million-row raw dataset. This report uses author/publisher statements and does not claim a new replication of those studies.','','The question receipt is a prespecified extension after substantial prior discovery, not blind preregistration. Curated source summaries are short paraphrases; publisher full texts and source screenshots are not redistributed here. No causal or commercial hypothesis is upgraded to confirmed by these foreign-context studies.']
(OUT/'REPORT.md').write_text('\n'.join(md))
print(json.dumps(out))
